  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of the Libyan National Seismological Network (LNSN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project consists of carrying out mutually agreed activities between UNESCO and the LCRSSS related to the &quot;Establishment of the Libyan Digital Seismological Network&quot; (LDSN). The LNSN network was designed to monitor local, regional and teleseismic activities, as well as to provide high quality data for research projects both locally and on the regional and global scale. The LNSN consists of 15 stations (3 very broadband and 12 broadband), utilizing state of the art VSAT communication technology, and a Central Processing Center, located in the City of Ghariyan, in addition to 13 portable stations. Building scientific capacities of Libyan specialists is a major component of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
